      "source_pages": "4",
      "markscheme_pages": "10",
      "task_summary": "Use mathematical induction to prove Aₙ = n! for n ∈ ℤ⁺, given that lim_{x→∞} x^m e^(-x) = 0 for any m.",
      "primary_topic": "number_algebra.mathematical_induction",
      "secondary_topics": [
        "calculus.integration_applications"
      ],
      "method_family": "mathematical_induction",
      "method_tags": [
        "base_case",
        "induction_hypothesis",
        "integration_by_parts",
        "induction_step",
        "conclusion"
      ],
      "method_path": [
        "Base case n=1: verify A₁ = 1 = 1!",
        "Induction hypothesis: assume A_k = k! = ∫₀^∞ x^k e^(-x)dx",
        "Induction step n=k+1: write A_{k+1} = ∫₀^∞ x^{k+1} e^(-x)dx",
        "Integrate by parts: u = x^{k+1}, dv = e^(-x)dx → du = (k+1)x^k dx, v = -e^(-x)",
        "Obtain [-x^{k+1}e^(-x)]₀^∞ + (k+1)∫₀^∞ x^k e^(-x)dx",
        "Apply given limit: [-x^{k+1}e^(-x)]₀^∞ = 0",
        "Substitute induction hypothesis: (k+1)·k! = (k+1)!",
        "Conclude: true for n=1 and if true for n=k then true for n=k+1, therefore true for all n∈ℤ⁺"
      ],
      "accepted_alternatives": [
        "Accept starting induction at n=0 throughout the proof"
      ],
